# PHP: PHP Manual (PHP 8.3), Language Reference: Basic syntax, Types, Strings, Attributes; requirements/languages/php.md
name     php

keyword  abstract and as break callable case catch class clone const continue declare default do echo
keyword  else elseif empty enddeclare endfor endforeach endif endswitch endwhile enum extends final finally
keyword  fn for foreach function global goto if implements include include_once instanceof insteadof
keyword  interface isset list match namespace new or print private protected public readonly require
keyword  require_once return static switch throw trait try unset use var while xor yield
type     int float bool string array object iterable void mixed never self parent
builtin  true false null die exit count strlen str_replace sprintf printf implode explode array_map
builtin  array_filter array_keys array_values in_array is_null json_encode json_decode var_dump
fold-case

line-comment   // #
block-comment  /* */
string   " "  : escapes interp=dollar
string   ' '  : escapes
string   ` `  : escapes interp=dollar
escape        : x=2 octal=3 u-braces
sigil    $    : attr
operators  +-*/%&|^!<>=:?~.@
calls
hook     php
